  "text": "Let's start by analyzing the given information and using Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the roots of a polynomial to its coefficients.\n\n1. For the polynomial \\( P(x) = x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c \\) with roots \\( r, s, t \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   r + s + t = -a\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   rs + rt + st = b\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   rst = -c\n   \\]\n\n2. For the polynomial \\( Q(x) = x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c + 120 \\) with roots \\( r-2, s+5, t-1 \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   (r-2) + (s+5) + (t-1) = -a\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (r-2)(s+5) + (r-2)(t-1) + (s+5)(t-1) = b\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (r-2)(s+5)(t-1) = -(c + 120)\n   \\]\n\nFrom the first equation of \\( Q(x) \\):\n\\[\n(r-2) + (s+5) + (t-1) = r + s + t - 2 + 5 - 1 = -(a) - 2 + 4 = -a\n\\]\nThis is true, so the first equation is satisfied.\n\nFrom the second equation of \\( Q(x) \\):\n\\[\n(rs + rt + st) - 2(s + t + r) + 10(r + s + t) - 20 = b\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( r + s + t = -a \\) and \\( rs + rt + st = b \\):\n\\[\nb - 2(-a + r + s + t) + 10(-a) - 20 = b\n\\]\nSimplifying:\n\\[\nb - 2(-a) + 2a - 10a - 20 = b\n\\]\n\\[\nb + 2a - 10a - 20 = b\n\\]\n\\[\nb - 10a - 20 = b\n\\]\n\\[\n-10a - 20 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n-10a = 20\n\\]\n\\[\na = -2\n\\]\n\nFrom the third equation of \\( Q(x) \\):\n\\[\n(r-2)(s+5)(t-1) = -(c + 120)\n\\]\nExpanding the left side:\n\\[\n(rs + 5r - 2s - 10 + 5t - 2t - 10) = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + 5r - 2s + 3t - 20 = -(c + 120)\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( r + s + t = -a = 2 \\) and \\( rs = b = 6 \\):\n\\[\n6 + 5r - 2s + 3(2) - 20 = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\n6 + 5r - 2s + 6 - 20 = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\n-8 + 5r - 2s = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\n-8 + 5r - 2(2 - r) = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\n-8 + 5r - 4 + 2r = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\n7r - 12 = -(c + 120)\n\\]\n\\[\n7r - 12 = -c - 120\n\\]\n\\[\n7r + 108 = -c\n\\]\nSince \\( r = \\frac{-a - (-c)}{-a} = \\frac{c + 2}{-2} \\), substituting \\( r \\) back:\n\\[\n7 \\left( \\frac{c + 2}{-2} \\right) + 108 = -c\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\frac{7(c + 2)}{2} + 108 = -c\n\\]\n\\[\n-7c - 14 + 216 = 